<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frombork</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Frauenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frombork (German Frauenburg) is a small town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a>. From the 13th century it was the seat of the cathedral chapter of Warmia, whose fortified Gothic cathedral stands on a hill above the town. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolaus-copernicus">Nicolaus Copernicus</a> lived there as a canon for much of his life, wrote his work on the motion of the heavens there, and was buried in the cathedral in 1543.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frombork.jpg" alt="Frombork" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: QuercusGd · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frombok_Katedra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
